  "Reviewed table: lowercase node label or user tag to one of the 15 Discogs genres (GEN-037 to GEN-039, ADR-0021). Keys starting with _ are comments.",
  "Seeded from the Discogs genre and style list (each style under the genre Discogs files it under). A style Discogs files under two genres takes the first in the fixed order: Blues, Brass & Military, Children's, Classical, Electronic, Folk, World, & Country, Funk / Soul, Hip Hop, Jazz, Latin, Non-Music, Pop, Reggae, Rock, Stage & Screen.",
  "Order-rule outcome: trip hop to Electronic (Discogs also lists it under Hip Hop). Deliberate overrides for the owner's library: disco to Funk / Soul, new wave to Rock, acid jazz to Jazz (Discogs lists them under Electronic too, which the order rule would pick); dream pop, power pop, jangle pop, paisley underground, folk punk, folk metal to Rock; gospel to Funk / Soul; indie pop, new romantic to Pop; ska punk, dub to Reggae.",
  "Not Discogs styles, mapped manually (checked against the Discogs API 2026-10-16): nerdcore, geek rock, nerd music (Discogs has only Nerdcore Techno, under Electronic). Verified Discogs styles: Chiptune (Electronic), Filk (Folk, World, & Country), Video Game Music (Stage & Screen).",
  "Bare stored forms of kept tags that are not Discogs styles (TAG-076; the stored tag is the bare Wikidata label, GEN-031): electronic, dance, electronic dance, experimental, singer-songwriter, estrada, epic, trailer, liquid funk, euro disco, modern classical.",
  "Classification categories (music of ..., ethnic music) and nodes with no entry here inherit from their ancestors (GEN-038)."
